      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, something similar to the `SkWorkingFormatColorFilter` (at least in name).\n\nSo this would be something like:\n```\n  gainmapMathColorSpace \u003d baseImage-\u003ecolorSpace()-\u003emakeLinearGamma();\n  baseImageShader \u003d baseImage-\u003emakeShader(.)-\u003e\n                    makeWithWorkingSpace(gainmapMathColorSpace, kUPMA)\n  gainmapShader \u003d gainmapImage-\u003emakeShader(.)-\u003e\n                  makeWithWorkingSpace(nullptr, kUPMA)\n  ... create gainmapMathShader ...\n  return gainmapMathShader-\u003emakeWithoutWorkingSpace(gainmapMathColorSpace, kUPMA)\n```\n\nSo there the `makeWithWorkingSpace` converts everything to the specified format, then the `makeWithoutWorkingSpace` converts everything from the specified format to \"whatever the destination color space is\" (or potentially cancels out with a `makeWithWorkingSpace` in the next stage of the pipeline).\n\nFrom grasping around at the various `onProgram` implementations, I think this amounts to having the \"with[out]WorkingSpace\" override the SkColorInfo that gets passed around to children. (But that\u0027s me grasping).\n\nI\u0027m hesitant to move to `makeRawShader` for the gainmap because of the filtering (it\u0027s low-res and upscaled). Also, fortunately, all image formats that support gainmaps are opaque (for now).\n\nOnce all of that is taken care of, we could make this take SkShaders for the base and gainmap, and take an explicit SkColorSpace to be linearized for the working space.",
